    "question": {
      ":question/id": "960d5147-f09b-5592-a6b7-40895ac5ee17",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y &=1 \\\\ 6x+3y &=6 \\\\ -4x-2y &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is inconsistent.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
