    "question": {
      ":question/id": "05273d92-8246-5530-8247-9d57fd906890",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+2y-3z &=4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x-3y+\\frac{1}{2}z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -3 & \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -3 & \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is one free variable, $z$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is consistent dependent.",
